WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.842
A clear graphic.

00:00:02.062 --> 00:00:03.223
A style of your own.

00:00:03.443 --> 00:00:05.150
And a source that comes with it.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:07.251
Welcome to Pollframe Studio.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.025
Let's design a Bundestag poll graphic for a post.

00:00:14.245 --> 00:00:16.753
In Studio, start by searching for the subject.

00:00:16.973 --> 00:00:20.804
The previews show different layouts using real data.

00:00:21.024 --> 00:00:23.903
Open a template that suits your post.

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:26.109
We'll choose Pollframe Original.

00:00:27.933 --> 00:00:30.093
Choose Edit to open the editor.

00:00:30.313 --> 00:00:33.146
The preview stays visible while you work on the
right.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:36.257
Give the graphic a short, factual headline.

00:00:36.477 --> 00:00:39.356
The typeface library previews each font.

00:00:39.576 --> 00:00:42.339
You can also adjust size and background.

00:00:42.559 --> 00:00:46.309
Values, party names, date and source stay protected.

00:00:46.529 --> 00:00:49.199
The design becomes yours, not the poll.

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:53.785
Save your design with a suitable name.

00:00:54.005 --> 00:00:56.478
This keeps the graphic and its settings.

00:00:56.698 --> 00:00:58.428
Would you like to reuse the look?

00:00:58.648 --> 00:01:00.540
Save a style as well.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.626
The wizard guides you through typeface, background
and sizes, one step at a time.

00:01:04.846 --> 00:01:08.875
Finally, review the summary and give your style a
name.

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:16.789
You'll also find your styles under My designs.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:18.959
They are saved in this browser.

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:23.730
For another graphic, open a different template and
choose Apply a style.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:27.027
The appearance transfers where it suits the graphic.

00:01:27.247 --> 00:01:34.283
Numbers, sources, axes and event selections are not
replaced by those from another graphic.

00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:38.188
A quick source check is part of the process.

00:01:38.408 --> 00:01:42.332
Info shows the pollster, date and record of the
reading.

00:01:42.552 --> 00:01:45.850
Further details explain the method and limits of
comparison.

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:51.666
You can copy a caption; the publication package
provides additional verification material.

00:01:51.886 --> 00:01:56.669
Pay particular attention to whether you are using a
single poll or a calculated historical

00:01:56.669 --> 00:01:57.041
series.

00:01:58.867 --> 00:02:01.665
For a fixed image, open PNG export.

00:02:01.885 --> 00:02:04.520
Check the format and legibility in the preview.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:09.129
An embed is for a website and can update with new
data.

00:02:09.349 --> 00:02:14.701
Choose deliberately: should your article show this
exact snapshot, or stay up to date?

00:02:14.921 --> 00:02:18.590
Before publishing, check the embedded content on a
phone too.

00:02:20.433 --> 00:02:25.495
That's the workflow: choose a template, design,
check sources and publish.

00:02:25.715 --> 00:02:27.712
Start with just one graphic.

00:02:27.932 --> 00:02:30.347
You can reuse your style later.

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:32.053
Enjoy Studio.
